CorvCAD patch series for KiCad 10.0.6 (caf7377), on top of 0009: let the push-and-shove
router's model interface (PNS_KICAD_IFACE_BASE) link without the board editor's view and tools.

Applied by integrations/kicad_core/fetch.py. Nothing changes in behaviour or in KiCad's own
builds.

pcbnew/router/pns_kicad_iface.cpp defines both PNS_KICAD_IFACE_BASE (board sync, rule
resolver, sizes, layers) and PNS_KICAD_IFACE, the editor's interface, which draws preview
items into the GAL view, hides items, reads the selection tool and pushes the editor's
commit. Every PNS_KICAD_IFACE member and the view-only PNS_PCBNEW_DEBUG_DECORATOR move
unchanged into a new pns_kicad_iface_view.cpp, listed after pns_kicad_iface.cpp in both router
source lists, and pns_kicad_iface.cpp drops the editor headers only they used (tool base,
selection tool, tool manager, GAL, painter, preview item). A program that only uses PNS_KICAD_IFACE_BASE (CorvCAD's headless router in
integrations/kicad_core/session/kicad_board.cpp) then links pns_kicad_iface.cpp without the
view and tool code.
